  "Description": "Demonstrates how to create 3D model text in Revit using the ModelText.ByTextSketchPlaneAndPosition node. This graph shows all the required inputs: text content, sketch plane for orientation, XYZ positioning coordinates, and model text type for formatting. Model text appears as a 3D element in the model space, visible from multiple views unlike regular text annotations.",
